arlier refusals had"] [78 1 "// spent it). A view held elsewhere, or dropped unreleased, is still the collector's question (exportsVerify). The"] [79 1 "// count found held is confirmed, as exportsVerify confirms it."] [83 3 "// within a finalizers' drain the resize is allowed as before (exportsVerify's rule): a __del__'s refusal"] [84 3 "// (_pyio.BytesIO.close's clear while a view is held) is then an unraisable BufferError whose traceback holds"] [85 3 "// the dying object past gc.collect() (test_memoryio's test_getbuffer_gc_collect)"] [88 17 "// the objects looked at, at most"] [175 1 "// Acquire and Release are a native's own export over a call (PyObject_GetBuffer ... PyBuffer_Release), for an"] [176 1 "// exporter whose buffer must not move while the call holds it."] [191 1 "// exportsOf is o's count, nil when o (or the built-in value of a subclass's instance) counts none."] [202 1 "// managedBuffer is _PyManagedBufferObject: one export of an exporter, shared by the views made from the first."] [204 23 "// the exporter's count (nil: the exporter counts none)"] [205 23 "// the views registered and not released (mbuf->exports)"] [206 2 "// a class's __buffer__ (PEP 688, slot_bf_getbuffer): the exporter and the view its __buffer__ returned, the"] [207 2 "// export held as typeobject.c's _PyBufferWrapper holds it (memory_getbuf of the view)"] [210 2 "// slot_bf_releasebuffer over a built-in exporter (queue 475): the object whose class's Python __release_buffer__"] [211 2 "// is called with a restricted view of master when the export goes, before the built-in's release (exp)"] [214 2 "// release is a Py_buffer's PyBuffer_Release (queue 473: a C exporter's view, kept in place; a memoryview's"] [215 2 "// __buffer__ export of itself), called once the last view goes"] [219 1 "// newManagedBuffer is the export memoryview(o) takes: o's count raised when it counts."] [223 3 "// PYI_NO_FINALIZERS: no view is ever found dead, so none counts (pyi's behaviour before 249)"] [230 1 "// register makes v a view of mb (mbuf_add_view): it holds the export until released or dead."] [241 1 "// drop is mbuf_release: the export given back once the last view went (PyBuffer_Release of the master: the exporter's"] [242 1 "// bf_releasebuffer)."] [244 40 "// slot_bf_releasebuffer: the Python method first, then the base's release"] [266 1 "// bufferwrapperReleasebuf is typeobject.c's bufferwrapper_releasebuf, then bufferwrapper_dealloc (queue 475): the"] [267 1 "// view __buffer__ returned gives its export back (memory_releasebuf); the class's Python __release_buffer__ is called"] [268 1 "// with that view when the view is not of the object itself (a view of the object, super().__buffer__'s, is released"] [269 1 "// by its own export's release, slot_bf_releasebuffer's, below). The wrapper then drops its reference to the view;"] [270 1 "// pyi has no reference counts, so a view of the object itself, which only the wrapper held in CPython's usual case"] [271 1 "// (__buffer__ returning super().__buffer__(flags)), is released here as its dealloc would, when nothing else exports"] [272 1 "// from it."] [276 2 "// a built-in's __buffer__ called on a subclass's instance gets the built-in value (a method descriptor's self)"] [286 2 "// its dealloc's mbuf_release: PyBuffer_Release of the object's own export, slot_bf_releasebuffer when the class's"] [287 2 "// __release_buffer__ is Python's (the export made of the built-in value has no slot of its own), then the base's"] [297 1 "// memoryviewFinalize is memory_dealloc's release of a view never released: its export given back."] [309 1 "// exportsVerify is the collection at a refused resize: Go's collection and the finalizers' drain (finRound) while it"] [310 1 "// gives exports back, within the collections' budget; whether e still exports (false also past the budget, or while"] [311 1 "// finalizers are draining: the resize then allowed). A count found held is confirmed until it moves."] [322 1 "// exportsCollect is exportsVerify's collection for any count of exports (n): false when it may not run (past its"] [323 1 "// budget, or while finalizers drain: the caller then goes on as if nothing were held), else whether n is still above"] [324 1 "// zero after the rounds (queue 595: also memoryview.release()'s, whose re-exporter dropped by del is found dead)."] [348 1 "// exportsRound is finRound's collection with a shorter wait: Go's collection, then a wait until a dead object is"] [349 1 "// queued or Go's finalizers have been still for 3 ms (polled every 100 us), then the drain. A view dropped unreleased"] [350 1 "// is queued as soon as Go's finalizer goroutine runs, so the common case (a temporary view) costs the collection"] [351 1 "// alone; a view still held costs the 3 ms once (BufferExports.confirmed)."] [375 2 "// exportsSpent is the time the refused resizes' collections took: held to a tenth of the elapsed wall time and"] [376 2 "// 200 ms, the moment at del's rule (finSpent, queue 222) with a budget of its own"] [378 2 "// PYI_EXPORTS_DEBUG=1: each verification's rounds on stderr"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[145 24] [150 28] [150 67] [193 32] [196 46] [244 24] [252 20] [254 16] [277 20] [292 23] [304 23] [334 16] [334 38] [356 28] [356 57] [364 28]]} (go/file "buffer_export.go" :imports [


